From: Mirdispo contributors
Subject: Fix two entries in the CEA mode table

Bit 10 of the CEA table is 1280x720p25, which the table spelled 1290x720.
Bit 16 is 1920x1080p24, which the table gave as 1920x1080p25, a second copy
of bit 12. A receiver that offers 1080p24 would have been sent a 25 Hz
stream in a session it agreed to at 24 Hz, had that mode been chosen.

diff -ruN a/src/wfd/wfd-video-codec.c b/src/wfd/wfd-video-codec.c
--- a/src/wfd/wfd-video-codec.c
+++ b/src/wfd/wfd-video-codec.c
@@ -14,13 +14,13 @@
   {1920, 1080, 30, FALSE},
   {1920, 1080, 60, FALSE},
   {1920, 1080, 60, TRUE},
-  {1290,  720, 25, FALSE},
+  {1280,  720, 25, FALSE},
   {1280,  720, 50, FALSE},
   {1920, 1080, 25, FALSE},
   {1920, 1080, 50, FALSE},
   {1920, 1080, 50, TRUE},
   {1280,  720, 24, FALSE},
-  {1920, 1080, 25, FALSE},
+  {1920, 1080, 24, FALSE},
   {3840, 2160, 24, FALSE},
   {3840, 2160, 25, FALSE},
   {3840, 2160, 30, FALSE},
